questions.prompt:
A teammate writes this to enforce a 10-character display-name limit and to show a preview:

```js
function tooLong(name) { return name.length > 10; }
function preview(name) { return name.slice(0, 5) + '…'; }
```

A user named `Ana 👩‍💻🎉🎉` complains. What goes wrong, and how would you fix both functions?

questions.answer:
```js
const seg = new Intl.Segmenter(undefined, { granularity: 'grapheme' });
const graphemes = s => [...seg.segment(s)].map(x => x.segment);
const tooLong = name => graphemes(name).length > 10;
const preview = name => graphemes(name).slice(0, 5).join('') + '…';
```

```js
function utf8Length(str) {
  let bytes = 0;
  for (const ch of str) {           // iterates code points
    const cp = ch.codePointAt(0);
    bytes += cp < 0x80 ? 1 : cp < 0x800 ? 2 : cp < 0x10000 ? 3 : 4;
  }
  return bytes;
}
utf8Length("hé€😀"); // 1 + 2 + 3 + 4 = 10
```
